The board of commissioners hereby authorizes the following persons to issue citations for violations of county ordinances:
(1) County sheriff and certified deputy sheriffs;
(2) County health department;
(3) County director of community development or his designee;
(4) Public works director or his designee;
(5) Animal control officers; and
(6) Other such officials as may be designated from time to time by the board of commissioners.
(Code 1991, § 2-5; Res. of 4-10-1985; Res. of 2-10-1992)

240:
All investments of the county shall adhere to O.C.G.A. § 36-83-4, and the county may invest and re-invest any money subject to its control and jurisdiction in:
(1) Obligations of this state or of other states;
(2) Obligations issued by the United States government;
(3) Obligations fully insured or guaranteed by the United States government or a United States government agency;
(4) Obligations of any corporation of the United States government;
(5) Prime bankers' acceptances;
(6) The local government investment pool established by O.C.G.A. § 36-83-8;
(7) Repurchase agreements; and
(8) Obligations of other political subdivisions of this state.
(Code 1991, § 2-253; Ord. No. 2011-06, 10-25-2011)
